      "text": "The memory cap was made ASan-safe: RLIMIT_AS is skipped when an ASan target is auto-detected or --no-memory-limit is set (since ASan reserves ~20 TB of virtual address space), relying on an external cgroup cap, while core-dump/nproc/nice limits are kept in all cases."
